@startuml technical-data-synchronization
title Data Synchronization Technical Process (24 nodes - under 25 limit)

' This example demonstrates a TECHNICAL PROCESS diagram with higher complexity
' Technical processes allow up to 25 nodes (vs. 10 for business processes)
' Audience: Developers and technical teams

skinparam activityBackgroundColor #E6F3FF
skinparam activityBorderColor #0066CC

|Data Sync Service|
start
:Initialize Sync Job;
note right
  Node 1: Load configuration
  Technical: Load sync_config.json
end note

:Connect to Source Database;
note right
  Node 2: Oracle DB connection
  Connection string: PROD_DB
end note

:Connect to Target Database;
note right
  Node 3: PostgreSQL connection
  Connection string: TARGET_DB
end note

if (Both Connections Valid?) then (yes)
  note right: Node 4 (decision)

  :Query Source Tables;
  note right
    Node 5: SELECT from T_CUSTOMER, T_ORDER
  end note

  :Calculate Delta;
  note right
    Node 6: Compare timestamps
    WHERE modified_date > last_sync
  end note

  if (Delta Found?) then (yes)
    note right: Node 7 (decision)

    :Transform Data Schema;
    note right
      Node 8: Oracle → PostgreSQL mapping
      Convert datatypes, field names
    end note

    :Validate Data Integrity;
    note right
      Node 9: Check constraints
      NULL checks, foreign keys
    end note

    if (Validation Passed?) then (yes)
      note right: Node 10 (decision)

      :Begin Transaction;
      note right: Node 11: START TRANSACTION

      :Acquire Row Locks;
      note right
        Node 12: SELECT FOR UPDATE
        Lock target rows
      end note

      :Execute UPSERT Operations;
      note right
        Node 13: INSERT ON CONFLICT UPDATE
        Batch size: 1000 rows
      end note

      :Update Audit Log;
      note right
        Node 14: INSERT INTO sync_audit_log
        Log sync metadata
      end note

      :Commit Transaction;
      note right: Node 15: COMMIT

      :Release Locks;
      note right: Node 16: Release row locks

      :Update Sync Status;
      note right
        Node 17: UPDATE sync_status
        SET last_sync = NOW()
      end note

      :Send Success Notification;
      note right
        Node 18: Kafka event
        Topic: data-sync-success
      end note

      :Update Metrics;
      note right
        Node 19: Increment sync_success_count
        Update Prometheus metrics
      end note

      :Log Success;
      note right
        Node 20: Log to application.log
        Level: INFO
      end note

      stop
      note right: Node 21 (end - success path)

    else (no - validation failed)
      :Rollback Transaction;
      note left
        Node 22: ROLLBACK
        Undo partial changes
      end note

      :Log Validation Errors;
      note left
        Node 23: Log constraint violations
        Level: ERROR
      end note

      :Send Failure Notification;
      note left
        Node 24: Kafka event
        Topic: data-sync-failure
      end note

      stop
      note left: End (failure path)
    endif

  else (no - no delta)
    :Log No Changes;
    note left: Node 22: No sync needed
    stop
    note left: End (no-op path)
  endif

else (no - connection failed)
  :Log Connection Error;
  note left: Technical: DB connection timeout
  stop
  note left: End (error path)
endif

legend right
  **TECHNICAL PROCESS NODE COUNT**: 24 nodes (EXCEEDS 15-node limit - requires splitting)

  **Node Breakdown**:
  - Start: 1 node
  - Process steps: 17 nodes (Initialize, Connect Source, Connect Target, Query, Calculate Delta,
                    Transform, Validate, Begin Tx, Acquire Locks, Execute UPSERT, Update Audit,
                    Commit, Release Locks, Update Status, Send Notification, Update Metrics, Log Success)
  - Decision points: 3 nodes (Connections Valid?, Delta Found?, Validation Passed?)
  - End: 1 node (primary success path)
  - Additional error handling: 3 nodes (Rollback, Log Errors, Send Failure)

  **Total**: 1 + 17 + 3 + 1 + 3 = 25 nodes (if all paths included)
  **Primary Path**: 21 nodes (EXCEEDS 15-node limit) ❌

  **ACTION REQUIRED**: Split into sub-diagrams
  - Main diagram: High-level sync workflow (≤15 nodes)
  - Sub-diagram 1: Database connection and delta calculation (≤15 nodes)
  - Sub-diagram 2: Data transformation and validation (≤15 nodes)
  - Sub-diagram 3: Transaction execution and monitoring (≤15 nodes)

  **Technical Details**:
  - Database: Oracle (source) → PostgreSQL (target)
  - Batch Size: 1000 rows
  - Transaction: ACID-compliant with row locking
  - Monitoring: Kafka events + Prometheus metrics
  - Error Handling: Rollback on validation failure

  **Source Traceability**:
  - Phase 1 DataSyncService.java:156-234
  - Phase 2 dependencies.puml (Oracle → PostgreSQL integration)
  - Phase 3 TECH-RULE-015 (Data integrity validation)

  **Audience**: Developers, Database Administrators, DevOps Engineers

  **NOTE**: This example demonstrates a technical process that EXCEEDS the 15-node limit
  and serves as a reference for identifying when sub-diagram splitting is required.
endlegend

@enduml
